{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765297,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"light-blue-dark_un","paid":0,"title":"Rapid Chess Tournament","festival_id":520757,"organization_id":821,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-03T23:59:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-15T13:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/rapid-chess-tournament-ieee-day26-ieee-mait-maharaja-agrasen-institute-of-technology-mait-new-delhi-1765297","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Chess Tournament | IEEE DAY&rsquo;26<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Get ready to put your strategy, calculation and decision-making skills to the test at the <strong>IEEE DAY&rsquo;26 Rapid Chess Tournament<\/strong>, organized by IEEE MAIT Student Branch.<\/li>\n<li>The competition will bring together college students for an intense on-campus chess showdown featuring a <strong>10+2 Rapid time control<\/strong> and a <strong>single-elimination knockout format<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Registrations are limited to <strong>100 participants<\/strong>, with <strong>64 players advancing to the main knockout tournament<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Official Participant Communication:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All registered participants must join the official <strong>IEEE DAY&rsquo;26 Chess Tournament WhatsApp group<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Important updates regarding selection of the Top 64 participants, reporting time, venue, tournament schedule, pairings and other announcements will be communicated through the group.<\/li>\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/chat.whatsapp.com\/HK1ek6jUqo94YCbIkblPb1?mode=gi_t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Join the Official Chess Tournament WhatsApp Group<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date:<\/strong> 15th October 2026<\/li>\n<li><strong>Venue:<\/strong> Maharaja Agrasen Institute of Technology, New Delhi<\/li>\n<li><strong>Mode:<\/strong> Offline<\/li>\n<li><strong>Participation:<\/strong> Individual<\/li>\n<li><strong>Maximum Registrations:<\/strong> 100 Participants<\/li>\n<li><strong>Main Tournament:<\/strong> Top 64 Participants<\/li>\n<li><strong>Format:<\/strong> Single-Elimination Rapid Knockout<\/li>\n<li><strong>Time Control:<\/strong> 10 minutes + 2 seconds increment per move (10+2)<\/li>\n<li><strong>Prize Pool:<\/strong> \u20b95,000<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Tournament Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The main tournament will consist of <strong>64 participants<\/strong> competing in a single-elimination knockout format.<\/p>\n<p>The progression will be:<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round of 64 &rarr; Round of 32 &rarr; Round of 16 &rarr; Quarterfinals &rarr; Semifinals &rarr; Final<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The winner of each match advances to the next round, while the losing player is eliminated from the tournament.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Selection for Main Tournament:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>A maximum of <strong>100 participants<\/strong> may register for the competition.<\/li>\n<li>From the registered participants, the <strong>Top 64 players will be selected based on their chess rating<\/strong> and will advance to the main knockout tournament.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are therefore required to provide their <strong>FIDE rating and\/or Chess.com\/Lichess rating<\/strong>, wherever applicable, during registration.<\/li>\n<li>In case a participant does not have an official FIDE rating, the organizing team may consider the submitted online chess rating or other available rating information for shortlisting.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Gameplay:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The tournament will follow a <strong>Rapid Chess format<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Each player will receive <strong>10 minutes of base time with a 2-second increment after every move (10+2)<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>The tournament will follow a <strong>single-elimination knockout format<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Players must report at the venue within the communicated reporting time.<\/li>\n<li>The <strong>touch-move rule<\/strong> will be applicable during matches.<\/li>\n<li>Players must operate their chess clock correctly after every move.<\/li>\n<li>Mobile phones, chess engines, external assistance or any other unfair means during a match are strictly prohibited.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are expected to maintain fair play and proper conduct throughout the tournament.<\/li>\n<li>Draw claims such as repetition, stalemate and other applicable chess rules will be handled according to the tournament rules and the decision of the tournament officials.<\/li>\n<li>Participants arriving after the permitted reporting\/match time may be subject to forfeiture.<\/li>\n<li>Any dispute arising during a match must immediately be brought to the attention of the tournament officials.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the <strong>Chief Arbiter \/ Tournament Officials<\/strong> regarding match-related disputes will be final.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must carry a valid <strong>college ID card<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to college students.<\/li>\n<li>Participation is individual.<\/li>\n<li>Participants from different colleges are welcome to register.<\/li>\n<li>A valid college ID may be required for verification at the venue.<\/li>\n<li>Registration must be completed within the specified registration window.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Registration Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration Deadline:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>14th October 2026<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Maximum Registrations:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>100 Participants<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Main Tournament Capacity:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>64 Participants<\/li>\n<li>Once registrations are closed and the final Top 64 are confirmed, further details will be communicated through the official WhatsApp group.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h2>Important Participant Guidelines<\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must complete their registration through Unstop.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must join the official WhatsApp group after registering.<\/li>\n<li>Players should report according to the schedule communicated by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are responsible for checking official updates before the tournament.<\/li>\n<li>Failure to report on time may result in forfeiture of the participant&rsquo;s slot.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must follow the instructions of the organizing team and tournament officials throughout the event.<br \/><strong><br \/><\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Important Note: Accommodation will not be provided by the organizers. Participants are required to make their own stay arrangements, if needed.<\/strong><\/p>","overall_prizes":"Cash prizes worth \u20b95,000 for the top 3 participants.","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":9094295,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-03T15:33:11+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-04T19:23:23+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"p7zZ89j","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":7,"checked":null,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":50,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-10-03 23:55:59","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":true,"closed_at":null,"linkedInEventId":"","teams":[],"players":[],"logoUrl":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/75x75\/uploadedManual-6ac0d2f02a417_ieee-day-logo-color-rgb.jpg","logoUrl2":"https:\/\/d